{"uid":"2415d7624b2a12cd","name":"test_logs_follow_shows_tool_invocation_before_tool_ends","fullName":"tests.test_cli_logs_follow_liveness#test_logs_follow_shows_tool_invocation_before_tool_ends","historyId":"4a66dc597da6dc4fc8c6137c61d6ddc7","time":{"start":1791881260648,"stop":1791881263601,"duration":2953},"description":"task 004: the live invocation line for a tool call must be visible\n    in the follow stream strictly BEFORE the matching `tool_execution_end`\n    is even emitted by the stub job, i.e. while the tool call is still\n    genuinely in flight -- not merely rendered-before-printed-completion\n    due to buffering.\n\n    approach-4 task 010: the window that proves this is now opened\n    DETERMINISTICALLY by `STUB_TOOL_HOLD_FILE` (tests/stub-pi/pi), which\n    blocks the stub between `tool_execution_start` and `tool_execution_end`\n    until this test releases it, instead of by a fixed `STUB_TOOL_SLEEP`\n    wall-clock gap. The old shape measured its 2.0s gap from the stub's own\n    emission but started its 1.5s no-completion check only once the\n    invocation line had traversed pump -> output.jsonl -> the engine's\n    0.3s-poll follower -> the CLI's renderer, so any delivery/scheduling\n    lag above 0.5s put `tool_execution_end` inside the check window and the\n    node went red with `'  ↳ ✓ ok (ok)'` -- observed on the\n    `ubuntu:24.04, PYTHONUSERBASE unset` nightly cell at 7b0860b (check run\n    103003362434, a 19-minute serial fast tier). With the hold there is no\n    margin to lose: the completion event cannot exist until this test says\n    so, and the assertions below are unchanged in strength.","descriptionHtml":"<p>task 004: the live invocation line for a tool call must be visible<br />\nin the follow stream strictly BEFORE the matching <code>tool_execution_end</code><br />\nis even emitted by the stub job, i.e. while the tool call is still<br />\ngenuinely in flight -- not merely rendered-before-printed-completion<br />\ndue to buffering.</p>\n<pre><code>approach-4 task 010: the window that proves this is now opened\nDETERMINISTICALLY by `STUB_TOOL_HOLD_FILE` (tests/stub-pi/pi), which\nblocks the stub between `tool_execution_start` and `tool_execution_end`\nuntil this test releases it, instead of by a fixed `STUB_TOOL_SLEEP`\nwall-clock gap. The old shape measured its 2.0s gap from the stub's own\nemission but started its 1.5s no-completion check only once the\ninvocation line had traversed pump -&gt; output.jsonl -&gt; the engine's\n0.3s-poll follower -&gt; the CLI's renderer, so any delivery/scheduling\nlag above 0.5s put `tool_execution_end` inside the check window and the\nnode went red with `'  ↳ ✓ ok (ok)'` -- observed on the\n`ubuntu:24.04, PYTHONUSERBASE unset` nightly cell at 7b0860b (check run\n103003362434, a 19-minute serial fast tier). With the hold there is no\nmargin to lose: the completion event cannot exist until this test says\nso, and the assertions below are unchanged in strength.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791880795156,"stop":1791880795157,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791880795157,"stop":1791880795157,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791881260632,"stop":1791881260637,"duration":5},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":179188